{
    "background_story": "Carter was a bright and adventurous young boy who loved trying new foods. However, after a series of mysterious stomachaches and fatigue, his parents took him to see a doctor. The diagnosis was unexpected: Carter had celiac disease, a condition that made him severely intolerant to gluten. At first, the news was daunting, and Carter felt like he was losing his freedom to enjoy his favorite treats. But with the support of his family, he learned to navigate the world of gluten-free living. Carter's parents helped him discover new recipes and restaurants that catered to his dietary needs. As he grew older, Carter became an advocate for celiac awareness, sharing his story to help others understand the importance of gluten-free options. His resilience and adaptability inspired those around him, and he proved that even with dietary restrictions, life could be full of flavor and joy.",
